Suppose that \( \bs x = (x_n: n \in \N) \) is a sequence of real numbers, and that \( a, \, b \in \R \) with \( a \lt b \). Define \( t_0(\bs x) = 0  \) and then recursively define
	\begin{align*} 
		s_{k+1}(\bs x) & = \inf\{n \in \N: n \ge t_k(\bs x), x_n \le a\}, \quad k \in \N \\
		t_{k+1}(\bs x) & = \inf\{n \in \N: n \ge s_{k+1}(\bs x),  x_n \ge b\}, \quad k \in \N
	\end{align*}

